(a) No licensee of a retail establishment under this article shall sell or offer for sale or display or keep in stock at his place of business where distilled spirits are offered for sale any other product of commodity except the following:
(1) Wines, but only if the licensee holds a valid and current license to sell wine at the place of business;
(2) Malt beverages or beer, but only if the licensee holds a valid and current license to sell malt beverages or beer at the place of business;
(3) Tobacco products;
(4) Beverages containing no alcohol and commonly used to dilute distilled spirits;
(5) Ice to be sold in sealed containers only; and
(6) Paper, styrofoam, glass or plastic cups or glasses in unbroken packages containing at least ten items each.
(b) Should such licensee elect to sell malt beverages or beer as provided in subsection (a)(2) of this section, such retail dealer shall be subject to all laws and regulations pertaining to the sale of distilled spirits, including but not limited to hours of sale and days of sale.
(c) Beverages containing no alcohol and commonly used to dilute distilled spirits as provided in subsection (a)(4) of this section may be dispensed through the use of vending machines, but no alcoholic beverage shall be dispensed through such vending machine.
(Ord. No. 771, § 1(4-99), 12-16-1997)

